<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine central bank sells dollars-traders.</title>
<headline>Philippine central bank sells dollars-traders.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine central bank stepped into the market early on Monday to sell dollars, traders said.</p>
<p>Traders said the central bank intervened starting at 28.25 down to 28 after the peso opened at 28.40.</p>
<p>Volume reached $5 million after more than 30 minutes of trading, with central bank sales amounting to $500,000 per transaction, traders said.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom (63 2) 841-8937</p>
</text>
